# The build context: what `docker build` sends, and what the builder stage's
# `COPY . .` copies. The image fetches its own ONNX Runtime, tokenizer and model
# (docker/Dockerfile), so it needs the source and nothing local.
#
# Without this file the context was the whole checkout: an .env holding real
# credentials went into the builder stage's layers, and two gigabytes of
# benchmark data went over the wire on every build.
.git
.env
.env.*
.benchmark-data
.tools
.models
.remember
.claude
.agents
.superpowers
data
*.out
*.test

# The backoffice's dependencies, build output and caches. Without these the
# build context carries every npm package and every .pyc, and each image builds
# its own dependencies anyway. The Python patterns are unanchored for the same
# reason as in .gitignore: a __pycache__ appears beside every package the
# interpreter touches.
backoffice/frontend/node_modules/
backoffice/frontend/dist/
backoffice/frontend/coverage/
backoffice/backend/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
